From: Adam Matthews <52178922+adamsthws@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] esp32c3 wifi: the signal strength keeps its minus sign

The fork added 96 to the strength of every frame the plug received, so the
-25 dBm of the plug's network reached the firmware as +71 to +80 dBm, and the
firmware passes it on as it is: the conversion's report said "Plug Wi-Fi
signal: 72 dBm", where runs on the real plugs recorded -44 to -52 dBm. A frame
now carries its access point's own strength, as the hardware gives it, plus
the fork's jitter of up to 9 dB: -25 to -16 dBm for the plug's network.
Offered upstream as lcgamboa/qemu #16.
---
 hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c b/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
index 6b14720..a6f548c 100644
--- a/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
+++ b/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
@@ -153,7 +153,11 @@ void Esp32_sendFrame(Esp32WifiState *s, mac80211_frame *frame,int length, int si
     memset(header,0,sizeof(wifi_pkt_rx_ctrl_c3_t)+length);
     wifi_pkt_rx_ctrl_c3_t *pkt=(wifi_pkt_rx_ctrl_c3_t *)header;
     *pkt=(wifi_pkt_rx_ctrl_c3_t){
-        .rssi=(signal_strength+(rand()%10)+96),
+        /* Autoflash emulator: the signal in dBm, as the hardware gives it - the
+         * access point's own strength (-25 dBm for the plug's network), give
+         * or take. The fork added 96, and the firmware passes the value on
+         * as it is: Tasmota reported +71 to +80 dBm, which no Wi-Fi gives. */
+        .rssi=(signal_strength+(rand()%10)),
         .rate=11,
         .sig_len=length,
         .sig_len_copy=length,
